################################################################################

==============================================================================
  RAIL CONFIGURATION
==============================================================================

  Rail Name   VDD
  Nominal     1.0000 V
  Rail R      0.35 Ω  (lumped model)
  Wire Area   0.1 µm²
  Nodes       8  (pg_voltage[7:0])

  Healthy node  :  pg_voltage[i] = 1  (voltage within spec)
  Drooping node :  pg_voltage[i] = 0  (voltage drooped below spec)

==============================================================================
  RAIL HEALTH — SCENARIO SUMMARY
==============================================================================

  SCENARIO  pg_voltage (hex)   DROOPING  HEALTHY  RAIL_STATUS
  --------  ----------------   --------  -------  -----------
  S1        0xFF  (11111111)      0/8      8/8      NOMINAL
  S2        0xFF  (11111111)      0/8      8/8      NOMINAL
  S3        0xF5  (11110101)      2/8      6/8      DEGRADED  ⚠
  S4        0x55  (01010101)      4/8      4/8      STRESSED  ⚠
  S5        0x03  (00000011)      6/8      2/8      CRITICAL  ✗
  S6        0x55  (01010101)      4/8      4/8      STRESSED  ⚠
  S7        0xFF  (11111111)      0/8      8/8      NOMINAL
  S8        N/A   (enable=0)      0/8      8/8      NOMINAL
  S9        0xFF  (11111111)      0/8      8/8      NOMINAL

==============================================================================
  DROOPING NODE DETAIL — SCENARIO 5 (WORST CASE)
==============================================================================

  pg_voltage = 0x03 = 0b00000011

  NODE     BIT    VOLTAGE_STATUS   ACTION
  ------   ---    --------------   ------
  VDD[0]   1      HEALTHY          —
  VDD[1]   1      HEALTHY          —
  VDD[2]   0      DROOPING         Flagged → violation_nodes count
  VDD[3]   0      DROOPING         Flagged → violation_nodes count
  VDD[4]   0      DROOPING         Flagged → violation_nodes count
  VDD[5]   0      DROOPING         Flagged → violation_nodes count
  VDD[6]   0      DROOPING         Flagged → violation_nodes count
  VDD[7]   0      DROOPING         Flagged → violation_nodes count

  violation_nodes (S5)  :  6 / 8
  drooping (RTL wire)   :  (~pg_voltage[0]) + ... + (~pg_voltage[7]) = 6

  FSM Response:
    drooping >= 4  →  high_act = 1  →  FSM transitions PROCESS → ALERT
    ALERT state    →  violation_nodes latched = 6
    ALERT exit     →  accum_load reset to 0 (A8 verified ✓)

==============================================================================
  RAIL DROOPING THRESHOLDS (FSM Logic)
==============================================================================

  Threshold       Value   Meaning
  ----------      -----   -------
  drooping >= 2    MED    FSM treats as medium activity (med_act=1)
  drooping >= 4    HIGH   FSM treats as high activity  (high_act=1)

  These thresholds are OR'd with switching activity index:
    high_act = (activity_index >= ACT_HIGH=10) || (drooping >= 4)
    med_act  = (activity_index >= ACT_MED=5)   || (drooping >= 2)

==============================================================================
  RAIL STRESS ACCUMULATION
==============================================================================

  toggle_budget tracks cumulative rail stress:
    Initial value   :  200
    Decrements by   :  activity_index per cycle (normal)
    Decrements by   :  W_ALERT=2 in ALERT state
    Never increases spontaneously (A12 verified ✓)

  Budget trace (end of each scenario):
    After S1   :  198  (minimal activity)
    After S2   :  190
    After S3   :  178
    After S4   :  142  (heavy 4-droop stress)
    After S5   :  136  (post-ALERT, budget=136 — ALERT deducted W_ALERT)
    After S6   :  136  (reset mid-test, same post-ALERT budget)
    After S7   :  136  (enable=0, no further depletion)
    After S8   :  136
    After S9   :  136  (FINAL)

  Budget Warning  (< 80) : NOT triggered in final state (136 > 80)
  opt_flags[4] — Widen Rails : NOT asserted

==============================================================================
  RAIL RECOVERY ANALYSIS
==============================================================================

  S7 — Recovery Scenario:
    enable=0, pg_voltage=0xFF, fa_a/b/cin=0
    repeat(20) @(posedge clk)

    After 20 idle cycles:
      violation_nodes  :  0 / 8  (all nodes recovered)  [PASS S7 ✓]
      ML IR Score      :  14 / 255  (< 60 warn threshold)  [PASS S7 ✓]
      FSM State        :  IDLE
      Alarm            :  0

    Recovery successful. Rail returns to NOMINAL within 20 clock cycles
    after stress removal (enable=0 gates activity: act_iso=0).

==============================================================================
  RAIL ANALYSIS CONCLUSION
==============================================================================

  Rail Violations (hard)       :  0  (no sustained droop events)
  Peak Drooping Nodes          :  6/8  (S5 — ALERT triggered and resolved)
  Final Drooping Nodes         :  0/8  (NOMINAL)
  Final Toggle Budget          :  136 / 200  (32% consumed)
  Rail Widen Recommendation    :  NOT required (budget > BUD_WARN=80)

  RESULT : PASS — Rail network healthy at simulation end.
           Transient stress in S5 correctly detected and cleared by FSM ALERT.

